Z||000000||Philphine||11-30-2000||12:01 PM||||<BR>i've gotten a rear gt facia i've been waiting for off ebay. i've been trying to find out if there is any type of rear spoiler extension like the chin spoilers you can get for the front. except for one thing i saw at a show (which i can't find either) i can't find any thing. so now i'm wondering if any one has a mod they've done themselves. i'd kind of like something like lower panel that lets the exhaust come through them. or maybe where the original exhaust area is covered, and/or have the licence plate in one of them and have the exhaust come out the middle or from where the licence plate was.<P>any strange or unusual ideas appreciated.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||11-30-2000||12:31 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/gallery/Cars/bee_fiero.jpg">  <P>I remember this Fiero, built by Pontiac, was in a HotRod magazine.  The opening areas for the exhaust areas were filled in by two bolt-on type plates, painted to match the car, and the exhaust ran out the middle of the car through 4 seperate pipes.  I found this pic of the car in the gallery, I'm sure someone will find and post a rear end shot.<P>I'm thinking it would be cool to build a dual exhaust so it ran flush out of holes/slots in those cover plates.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 11-30-2000).]||||reg||3
